# An empty body tube on the outside is aerodynamically a tube fin set (air flows through it): three Body tubes dragged onto the
# booster's side are open, the pod's Inspector says `Aero  Tube fins (open)` and Analyze counts a "Tube fins" component in the CP.
# Adding a nose cone to one of the pod bodies (a nose may go on the fore node of any body whose fore end is free) closes it: the
# pod becomes a `Body`.
#   cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/tubefins.drive out/tubefins
viewport 1280x800
click (142, 705)
press "Body tube"
move (300, 560)
move (500, 400)
move (700, 300)
move (767, 276)
release (767, 276)
screenshot build-open-tubes.png
click "Analyze"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot analyze-open-tubes.png
click "Build"
# The pod's tube is selected: a click on the Nose cone row puts the nose on that pod (the core already has its own).
click "Nose cone"
screenshot build-pod-nosed.png
click "Analyze"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot analyze-pod-nosed.png
